00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.160
Zoe: I had the experience of working
with a child with autism who really

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.639
enjoyed anything related to messy play.

00:00:13.209 --> 00:00:17.040
And through messy play, we were able
to help them to learn to communicate

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.310
through asking for different items,
and it was always a lot of fun.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.540
It was always very messy.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.050
I'd always be covered in whatever it
was they were interested in - from

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.280
like flour, to hot chocolate powder,
marshmallows, whatever it was.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.530
Paint anything.

00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:40.180
And it was always great fun, and it
really helped the student to learn how

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.330
to communicate because they got a lot of
enjoyment out of it, and they were always

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.260
very excited to  engage in anything messy

